; Test whether the first object has a single place
;
; Looks at the record of Noun1Record: its field +0 (N, the number of locations
; it lists) minus 1. Things with several places (doors, rivers, webs) have N > 1;
; ordinary portable objects and characters have N = 1. The attack handler
; #R$9171 uses the same test on the second object ("you cannot kill with X").
; .
; O:F Z set when N is 1
; O:IX Record of the first object
@label=CheckSinglePlace
c$9246 LD IX,($B708) ;
 $924A LD A,(IX+$00) ;
 $924D DEC A         ; Z when N = 1
 $924E RET           ;
